At f7880c9 decide.js implemented the sellability stage and reuse-first and
nothing downstream, so its decision vocabulary was five of the legacy engine's
eleven. On any campaign the legacy engine settled with one of the other six
gates, a live lane would have carried on and spent fresh accounts. The
coverage gate is the one that matters most — its wildcard bug once blocked all
farming — and a lane without it would re-buy accounts for demand already
covered. There was also a phantom disagreement: with a zero grant the lane said
`farm` with plannedAccounts 0, which compared as spend against a legacy
skip_no_accounts.

Unobserved because the comparison meant to catch it produced zero comparable
pairs.

decideCampaign now runs all six gates IN THE LEGACY ORDER (the comparison is
only meaningful if both engines stop at the same gate for the same inputs):

  sellability -> host -> reuse-first -> time -> coverage -> pool floor ->
  capacity -> reuse-only -> farm/probe

Every gate comes from the legacy engine's own helpers, exposed by one additive
hunk on autoFarmer.js's module.exports (probeHost, isForcedGame, manualFarmMap,
activeAutoBotCount, autoSeatCapacity, readyPoolQuery, WILDCARD_CREDIT_CAP,
COUNT_MANUAL_AS_COVERAGE). Nothing else in that file changes; the hunk must be
applied onto prod's copy, per FARM2-PLAN's deployment note.

The decision context legacy assembles once per tick (host probe, manual-bot
stash, owned set, archive coverage) is resolved lazily and memoised in the
cycle's shared hostCache, so lanes in one cycle share one host sweep, through
the SSH semaphore. It can also be handed in as legacy's ctx shape, which is how
the tests reach each gate without a host. Every gate is a read; a test asserts
a full pass writes nothing to AutoFarmTask or the pool.

One place leans on the SHAPE of a legacy query rather than calling it:
recycledPoolCount composes the recycled pass of claimPoolAccounts from its
exported primitives, because legacy settles reuse-only at claim time and a lane
needs it at decision time. Flagged in the doc.

targetAccounts now includes the market floor, as the legacy row's `wanted`
does and as the replay harness rebuilds.

decisionClasses: LANE_DECISIONS covers the full vocabulary. Kept as a separate
declaration so the tripwire (LEGACY_ONLY_DECISIONS, lane_missing_gate) fires
again the next time the two drift apart. Three vocabulary tests inverted to
assert the gap is closed.

21 new tests; the 87 existing farm2 tests pass. Suite 659/664 vs the same 5
pre-existing orphan-test failures.

Known gaps, in the doc: the stash sweep runs per 3-minute lane cycle vs
legacy's 10-minute tick; a LIVE lane's skips are still not written to
AutoFarmTask (pre-existing shape, needs its own change).
